WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.898 --> 00:00:02.040
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:03.610
- [Linda] Unless you're from New Orleans,

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.610
you would not know nothing
about the Hangover Hotline.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:10.230
- [Male] I feel like my
head is going to explode.

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:12.600
Can I please have some of your soup?

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.780
- Yes, I got that hangover cure.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.154
I'm on my way.

00:00:16.154 --> 00:00:19.154
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:25.340
My name is Chef Linda Green.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.340
I am called the Ya-Ka-Mein Lady.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:30.510
Ya-ka-mein is one of New
Orleans' best kept secret.

00:00:30.510 --> 00:00:32.440
It's a noodle soup.

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:36.470
Ya-ka-mein was classified
as a poor-man dish.

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.130
It is Chinese and
African-American fusion.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.630
It's good for the soul.

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:45.540
It's good for a hangover. (laughs)

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.450
Oh my God, when it hits the tongue,

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:48.910
it goes to the brain,

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.900
and then it come back to the tongue,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.057
and say, "I want more."

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.670
My mother was a cafeteria technician.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:05.843
I was a cafeteria technician, too.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:09.860
My mom and my grandmother
used to cook ya-ka-mein

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:11.580
and she always did tell me that

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:14.190
I may be able one day to use it,

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.600
and she was right.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.540
When Katrina hit,
everyone lost their jobs.

00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:24.443
I needed a job after I lost
my job with the school.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.850
I was catering, and I
was selling ya-ka-mein

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.110
at a lot of the festivals in the city.

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:33.330
I won Gumbo Festival.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:35.490
I won Sushi Festival.

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.730
I've been winning a lot.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:40.350
Now I've just been very
persistent and consistent

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.910
with this ya-ka-mein, and it became popular;

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.680
and the phone was ringing off the hook.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.550
Everybody used to say, "Where
the Ya-Ka-Mein Lady at?"

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.153
That's how I got that name.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.730
You know, people from
all over were calling me.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:57.180
There's a hotline there.

00:01:57.180 --> 00:02:00.260
I deliver or some will
come and pick it up.

00:02:00.260 --> 00:02:03.770
I went out on faith, and
I never looked back.

00:02:04.822 --> 00:02:07.822
(upbeat jazz music)

00:02:09.282 --> 00:02:10.550
I love my city, y'all.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:12.010
I'm not going to tell y'all a word of lie.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:13.380
I love my city.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.850
My name got known because a hangover

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.890
is very common in New Orleans.

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.830
Ya-ka-mein is the best remedy

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:23.590
for a New Orleans-sized headache.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.390
Everyone call it Old Sober.

00:02:26.390 --> 00:02:28.230
I just love what I do.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:30.030
I love cooking.

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:34.540
I love for someone to enjoy
my food, and I love for them

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:38.117
to come to me and tell me
everything was beautiful.

